course: dictionary
lesson: 5421
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it tell you which one you need. The word ladder is a noun for a tool you climb. «Çatalhöyük in Turkey was a town about 9,000 years ago with houses so tightly packed that people climbed in through holes with ladders.» The clue is climbed in through holes, so a ladder helps you reach a high place.
explain: A ladder is made of two long side pieces joined by steps called rungs. Ladder can also mean a series of levels you move up, like a career ladder. «Ben's teacher drew a «lie ladder»: one lie on the bottom rung, and every rung needs another lie to hold it up.» Here a ladder is a set of steps, one above another, so each rung is a level that rests on the one below.
explain: In British English, ladder is also a word for a line of broken threads in tights, and in the USA people say run. Check by swapping in your meaning. If the sentence still makes sense with a climbing tool, you have the right meaning. If it does not, try another meaning from the list.
fact: A ladder is a piece of equipment for climbing up and down.
fact: The steps on a ladder are called rungs.
fact: Safety rule: only use a ladder with an adult nearby, on flat, firm ground.
fact: «Snakes and Ladders» (Chutes and Ladders in the USA) is a board game where ladders take you up.
fact: In British English, a ladder is a line of broken threads in tights; in the USA this is called a run.
exercise: «People climbed in through holes with ladders.» What is a ladder here? | A line of broken threads in tights | A board game | A wooden house | *A tool for climbing up and down with steps
exercise: «A career ladder» is a series of levels you can move up. What does ladder mean here? | A line of broken threads | A tool for painting walls | *A series of levels you can move up | A bridge over a river
exercise: «My tights have a ladder in them.» What does ladder mean in British English? | A row of steps for climbing | A dream about heaven | *A line of broken threads | A board game for two players
test: What are the steps of a ladder called? | Wheels | Nails | *Rungs | Ropes
test: Where should a ladder stand, according to the safety rule? | On a moving boat | On soft, sloping mud | Leaning far to one side | *On flat, firm ground
exam: In British English, what does «ladder» mean in «My tights have a ladder in them»? | A row of levels at work | A tall tool for climbing up | A game for two players | *A line of broken threads in tights
